## Commercial lines agents' SSO sessions expired immediately due to misconfigured session timeout; fixed via SSO config update.

**Source:** HistoricalTicket (INC-400002)
**Module:** BillingCenter | **Category:** AuthenticationAccess | **Severity:** SEV2-High
**Resolution Type:** ConfigChange
**Date:** 2025-11-04

### Summary / Symptom
Agents in the commercial lines team are unable to log in after 2pm every day. The session expires immediately upon login. The issue started after a configuration change was pushed to the SSO provider last Thursday. Personal lines agents are unaffected.

### Resolution
The root cause was a misconfiguration in the SSO provider, where the session timeout for the commercial lines user group was set to 2 minutes instead of the intended 480 minutes. This caused sessions to expire immediately upon login for affected users. The issue was resolved by correcting the session timeout value in the SSO provider's admin console. After the change, commercial lines agents were able to log in and maintain active sessions as expected.


